.SH NAME
p106\-stats \- generate local statistics from municipal 106
reports_raw.json exports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p106\-stats
[\fB\-h\fR]
\fIcommand\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate local statistics from municipal 106 reports_raw.json exports.
Fully offline: files are read locally, outputs are written locally,
nothing is uploaded.
.PP
The build subcommand takes one or more export JSON files and writes
summary.json, the monthly/categories/streets CSVs and report.html into
\-\-output. Fully offline: no network, no credentials.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message and exit.
.SS Arguments
.TP
\fIcommand\fR

.SS "build options"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output directory for summary.json, the CSV tables and report.html.
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-top\-streets\fR \fITOP_STREETS\fR
How many streets to keep in by_street (default: 20) Default: 20.
.TP
\fB\-\-plates\-ledger\fR \fIPLATES_LEDGER\fR
Optional private filing\-ledger CSV; adds a repeat\-plates aggregate
(plates.csv with plate,reports for 3+ distinct filed reports) \- the
ledger itself never leaves the machine.
.TP
\fIinputs\fR
Reports_raw.json export file(s)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Summary.json, the CSV tables and report.html written to the output
directory; one summary line on stdout.
.TP
.B 1
Input error (missing, unreadable or invalid export file; or an
unreadable \-\-plates\-ledger file), \fBp106\-stats: ...\fR on stderr.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (argparse, or an invalid value such as \-\-top\-streets 0),
message on stderr.
